act destiny the action's furious the  moments are tense but those are barely  the main reasons why i find this fight  so good what i like the most about the  fight is the consequences of it both in  universe and to us viewers who had to  lay witness to such an emotional moment  yeah i know the fight had death flags  plastered all over it but has that ever  diminished the impact of a fight like  this for you i mean personally speaking  not much the fight may have been lenny  swansong but he'll always be remembered  such a great supporting character that  gave off a comforting aura this has been  an emotional end to his tale and the  feels came from a show that i didn't  expect them to come from  now given the premise of the show it's  obvious that we'll be getting at least  one awesome strategic fight from  platinum end battle royale anime with  supernatural beings has always been a  recipe for some cool combat and for  platinum and it holds up its side of the  bargain this is a fight that featured  quite a hefty use of cg now that doesn't  make it any less good as i still got my  heart pounding with how fast everything  moved it's quite hard to follow the  actual action but that only adds to the  moment with how wildly the camera angles  were you can really feel the intensity  of this showdown platinum end prides  itself on its premise of pitting world  views against each other both sides have  different viewpoints on killing people  and that puts some added stakes in this  already nice fight now what i want to  say that platinum end is a candidate for  anime of the season it's got some very  intriguing themes alongside the deeply  passionate fights  [Music]  [Music]  one piece stays strong with this next  fight luffy and x-drake versus numbers i  really like how one piece is so  seamlessly adapted to modern anime  techniques it's not a show with fights  as mind-blowing as ufo table or mapa  ones but they are still damn good we've  had that zorro moment not too long ago  and now we have this let's just say that  this pose animation for the series has  been insane the fight itself is simple  to be honest it's luffy showing how  strong he's becoming my destroying  opponents bigger than he is still let's  appreciate the effort that got put into  it you can really feel the impact of  each earth shattering attack the way the  whole thing gets presented and it caps  off with a key moment of drake asking to  join luffy's alliance now if a simple  fight like this got this amount of care  from the anime team imagine the latter  fights down the line tam i'm so excited  just thinking about them  if you've been watching my videos you  know that i've said a lot of good stuff  about dragon quest it's quite the niche  anime but i really like the nostalgic  feel it gives me it's also got some  nifty fights that 19 shonen fans would  like well what do you know dragon quest  does it again most notable in the fight  is how dye just parries every explosive  like it's nothing not quite ichigo  slashing away sembon zakura level but  it's still cool seeing the scene in  anime form the fight's quite standard  but i think it's the voice acting and  then the camera angles that make this  fight so good simply beautiful work in  presenting this fight it's very  impactful and attention-grabbing and  that finishing blow is just a thing of  beauty it's as shonen as it can be and  fans of the genre will definitely love  this fight now let's take a break then  shall we do you know what makes video  creators happy subscriptions so if you  haven't done so yet please make sure to  hit that subscribe button and get those  numbers up a million subs somewhere in  the middle of next year is the goal come  on let's do it together  versus hounds deserves a special mention  i'm not gonna lie here i almost  overlooked ranking of kings at the start  the simplistic art didn't appeal too  much and the premise didn't seem that  interesting to me to be honest but to my  surprise it ended up being one of the  best anime this season as i said in a  previous video that you can check out  another surprise came in the form of a  fight that i didn't see coming dorche  fighting beasts may not seem too  impressive in terms of its premise but  i'll just let the actual anime clip do  most of the talking i mean just look at  the level of detail there this is truly  some impressive battle animation and  you've got to give props to the studio  for making the fight so beautiful i mean  what am i saying it's wit we're talking  about here ranking of kings may not be  some battle anime where hype fights  abound when it comes to confrontations  like this the show doesn't disappoint  thanks to the level of detail and the  stakes that you can feel  sparky's always prided itself on those  insane fights that show off the  grittiness and the violence that people  have loved martial arts anime for bucky  continues to impress in his latest  season with this battle that pits our  main character against oliver now this  fight has what we've always loved about  barky the sheer unadulterated  over-the-top violence and intensity that  comes with every battle the insanity is  just off the charts with this battle and  both fighters do their share of flexing  on the others in a show of power this is  the fight where you can truly feel the  pressure and impact with each blow  connecting and that kind of presentation  really adds to the fight if you're up  for some good old smash mouth fighting  featuring monsters of men this could be  a good entry point for getting you to  start watching bucky  we never got a choji versus sasuke  fighting the original series but here we  are lots of good things can be said in  this showdown between best friends  sarada and chocho duking out already had  some emotional investment behind it the  actual fight is as cool as it gets  splitting hand-to-hand face-offs and the  unleashing of some old favorites makes  this great fan service for all-time fans  on a side note you can already see some  of the ujiha ruthlessness seeping  through in this fight even if she's  fighting her friend she'll be a  powerhouse when she's older but only  time will tell how destructive that  power can be remember karkashi's quote  about chidori yeah considering she  attempted the move on her friend i'd say  there's room for interesting  developments ahead  i honestly didn't expect the second  season of demon slayer to recap morgan  train in its first episode but the  moment that announcement was made one  thing became clear those of us who never  saw the movie in theaters would get the  chance to see one of the most hyped  fights of the past year in rengoku vs  akaza and knowing ufo table you know  they're already gonna do a damn good job  on it and let's just say i was simply  blown away how the fight translated into  the anime format it's got a lot of the  stuff we've come to love from demon  slayer fights like the special effects  the awesome animation and the intense  music and voice acting  you know it's been a long time coming  mushoku tensei has had some good fights  but i think that every major isekai  needs to have that big fight the one  with a lot of oomph that people will  always remember enter dragon god orsted  the battle waste no time getting to the  good parts kicking off with an intense  barrage that's all sorts of awesome if  you've still got doubts on how much care  is given to animating mushoku tensei  this fight should erase the last of  those doubts the others then get  involved in the fight but alstead  disposes of them all without breaking a  sweat overall the buildup of the tension  the sound direction and the post fight  repercussions make this battle so  awesome it's a squash match that looks  so unexpectedly cool but i personally  felt bad for how badly dead end got  destroyed i won't say i cried at the  scene but seeing the defeated dead end  gave me some of the strongest emotions i  felt this season so that's my list but  what about yours are there any other  fights that you really enjoyed from the  fall season come share with everyone on  the comment section if you can't get  enough of these lists and want more  check out the rest of my channel i've  got seasonal stuff decade stuff or just  lists that talk about certain moments  like villains showing their power and  flexing on the heroes all the times  heroes get betrayed and come back  stronger you can support the channel  through both my patreon and channel  memberships the links are down below you  might also want to drop by and give my  instagram a follow so that you'll get  the latest news and know what's going on  both in the world of anime and this  channel i had fun making this video and  i hope you had a good time watching it i  hope to see you again for the next video  and i wish you a great day

